	(text "IND-2 - buzzer, low-side driver"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 44.45 113.03 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0937d3c3-c2f9-48da-bb11-84648c1bec4d")
	)
	(text "Notes:\n- IND-1: LED references chosen 2026-08-15. D4 = KT-0603R red (C2286, Basic),\n  D5 = NCD0603Y2 yellow (C89811, Preferred-Extended, no feeder fee).\n  R13 / R14 = 1k: at 3V3 that is about 1.0-1.7 mA depending on the LED Vf,\n  which gives roughly 10-25 mcd - enough for an indoor status indicator.\n- IND-2: passive magnetic buzzer, PB5 = TIM3_CH2 so tones are free in firmware.\n- R17 = 5R1 (decided 2026-08-15): the MLT-8540 coil is a 3.6 V class part on a\n  post-OR rail near 4.6 V. 5.1 ohm leaves the coil at about 3.37 V at the\n  ~220 mA coil current, inside its 3.6 V rating, and also protects the coil\n  from a firmware bug leaving PB5 high, which a duty cap would not. No\n  fee-free 6.8 ohm 0805 exists at JLCPCB; 5R1 (C17724) is Basic and is the\n  fee-free option with the lowest resistor dissipation. 0805 for the\n  dissipation: about 0.25 W peak, so beeps must stay duty limited - a\n  continuous tone would blow past the 125 mW rating of an 0805.\n- R15 = 1k base resistor gives deep saturation at ~220 mA.\n- R16 = 10k base-to-GND keeps the buzzer silent while PB5 is high-Z at reset.\n- D6 (1N4148W) is across the coil, cathode to the 5 V side."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 107.95 158.75 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "5cc39343-ef3d-46e2-a6b8-26d99f1bebd6")
	)
	(text "Indicators - status LEDs (IND-1) and buzzer driver (IND-2)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 44.45 78.74 0)
		(effects
