				)
			)
		)
		(property "Notes" "Buzzer series resistor, decided 2026-08-15. The 8540 coil is a 3.6 V class part on a post-OR rail near 4.6 V: 5.1 ohm leaves the coil at about 3.37 V at the ~220 mA coil current, inside its rating, and also protects the coil from a firmware bug leaving PB5 high, which a duty cap would not. No fee-free 6.8 ohm 0805 exists at JLCPCB; 5R1 (C17724) is Basic and is the fee-free option with the lowest resistor dissipation. 0805 for the dissipation: about 0.25 W peak, so beeps must stay duty limited - a continuous tone would blow past the 125 mW rating of an 0805."
			(at 76.2 127 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
